		"description": "API - PP-6 - Create a Master Lloyd's Agreement and Link Underlying UMRs\n\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nGenerated: 2026-01-27T18:53:25.466Z (FeatureGenerator v3.1)\nUpdated: 2026-01-27 (Based on BA/Dev conversation and CMT structure)\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n## Setup Instructions:\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Create a new environment (or use existing Dynamics QA environment)\n3. Set the following environment variables:\n   - `d365_tenant_id`: Your Azure AD Tenant ID\n   - `d365_client_id`: Your Azure AD App Registration Client ID\n   - `d365_client_secret`: Your Azure AD App Registration Client Secret\n   - `d365_scope`: API scope (e.g., https://accelinsqatest.crm11.dynamics.com/.default)\n   - `d365_base_url`: Your Dynamics 365 instance URL (e.g., https://accelinsqatest.crm11.dynamics.com)\n   - `d365_api_version`: API version (e.g., v9.2)\n\n## Authentication:\n1. Run the \"🔐 Get Dynamics 365 Access Token\" request first\n2. The access token will be automatically saved to the `d365_access_token` collection variable\n3. All subsequent requests will use this token via Bearer authentication\n\n## Entity Sets:\n- Master Agreements: `accelins_masteragreements`\n- Contracts (CMT UMRs): `accelins_contracts` (or appropriate entity set name)\n\n## API Endpoints:\n- Base URL: `{{d365_base_url}}/api/data/{{d365_api_version}}/`\n- Create: POST `/accelins_masteragreements`\n- Get: GET `/accelins_masteragreements(<guid>)`\n- Update: PATCH `/accelins_masteragreements(<guid>)`\n- Query: GET `/accelins_masteragreements?$filter=...`",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
